# Access Reviews (ticket 15).
# Needs a Tenant Admin access token with an Active Tenant (see http/tenants.http), an enabled
# Application with some active Role Assignments (see http/role-assignments.http), and a Registered
# Resource of it for the per-resource view (see http/registered-resources.http).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@tenantToken = paste-tenant-admin-access-token
@applicationId = paste-enabled-application-id
@reviewId = paste-review-id
@itemId = paste-item-id
@otherItemId = paste-another-item-id
@resourceId = paste-registered-resource-id
@roleAssignmentId = paste-role-assignment-id-under-review

### Start a review of one enabled Application, due at dueAt (with a time zone, in the future, within
### 365 days). Every Role Assignment active in it now becomes an item. 409 if one is already open
### for the Application, if it isn't enabled, or if nobody holds a Role in it; 404 for an unknown one.
### Writes access_review.started.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}", "dueAt": "2026-12-09T12:00:00Z" }

### 400: dueAt in the past
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}", "dueAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z" }

### Reviews, newest first, each with progress { total, pending, certified, revoked, autoRevoked }.
### Filters: status (open, closed), applicationId. Paginated: limit, cursor.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews?status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### One review and its progress. pastDue is true once the due date has passed but the Scheduler
### hasn't closed it yet.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Its items, by member email then Role name. Each has outcome (pending, certified, revoked,
### auto-revoked), decidedAt and decidedByName. Filter: outcome. Once closed, this is the outcome report.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Only the undecided ones
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}/items?outcome=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Certify an item: its Role Assignment stays. Any Tenant Admin can decide any item. Writes
### access_review.item_certified. 409 once decided, after the due date, or if the assignment expired.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}/items/{{itemId}}/certify
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### 409: already decided
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}/items/{{itemId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Revoke an item: its Role Assignment ends at once (role_assignment.revoked with accessReviewId)
### and the item is recorded as revoked (access_review.item_revoked).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/access-reviews/{{reviewId}}/items/{{otherItemId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### The per-Registered-Resource view: each row now lists the member's active Role Assignments in the
### Application (assignments: { id, role, expiresAt, decidesAnswer, pendingReviewItemId }), and
### openReview names the open review of the Application.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/registered-resources/{{resourceId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Revoking from that view revokes the underlying Role Assignment, and decides its pending review
### item as revoked by the same Tenant Admin. So does revoking it on the Role Assignments page,
### deleting its Role or removing its Membership.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/role-assignments/{{roleAssignmentId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### At the due date: within a minute, the Scheduler revokes each undecided item's Role Assignment
### (endReason auto-revoked, no actor), records the item as auto-revoked and closes the review.
### To try it, start a review due a minute or two ahead and wait.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?eventType=access_review.item_auto_revoked
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### The closing entry carries the final counts.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?eventType=access_review.closed
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### The chain still verifies with every decision in it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events/integrity
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
